((date 2026-10-13) (slug short-wide-top)
 (hypothesis
  "Wide-top short screen (pre-registration dev/plans/short-wide-top-screen-2026-10-13.md, commit 6a0177107, merged #3299; user option (b) after the setup-map no-build): does a price-defined wide top short beat an SPY short? H = a 52-week-high week with close >= 30-week MA (late Stage 2); breakdown i in [H+8, H+52] with close < lowest close of [H-8, i-1], close < 30w MA, MA(i) <= MA(i-4). Entry next adjusted open; stop 1.01 x highest high of [H+1, i-1]. PIT top-3000 v12, close >= $5 (sensitivity $17), 2000-2025, one event per symbol per 182 days. Rule: O1 +60 beat < 55 % or median <= 0 -> CLOSE; else O2 edge criteria as the setup map. Proxy screen: may conclude only build or no-build.")
 (base_scenario
  "short-wide-top-2026-10-13: offline event screen, host awk over data/ bars; 24,790 events in results/events/<year>.csv; scripts/run.sh regenerates; analyst null and traces in results/analysis/ (run_all.sh)")
 (window_id top3000-pitv12-2000-2025-wide-top-events) (baseline_label spy-short)
 (variants (((label widetop-O1-60) (config_hash short-wide-top) (aggregate ()))))
 (verdict Reject)
 (notes
  "NO-BUILD DECISION (CLOSE at step 1; proxy screen; nothing built, nothing retires). O1 +60 n=24,790 beat 51.3 % (week-clustered CI 50.3-52.4) median +0.50 %; $17 floor beat 50.8 %. WHY: (1) the far stop (median room 38 %, 18.5 % stopped) makes O2 the no-stop hold, so this re-measures the setup map's coin flip (+0.50 % / 51.3 % vs +0.49 % / 51.4 %); (2) the coin flip is the universe: against a calendar-matched random top-3000 member null (864,415 draws), 49.1 % of events beat the date's null median at +60 bars (setup map 49.1 % too) - a broken top carries no information about the next 1-6 months relative to SPY; (3) the 2013-25 beat of 56 % and the bull-tape beat are the cap-weight/size base rate (null 57.0 %; 43-66 % by year); (4) the book's timing window is adverse: early SPY Stage 4 events 45.4 % vs null. More price-shape short screens are not worth prioritizing; short interest is the one book lever left (data-gated: free FINRA exchange-listed only from 2021-06; EODHD fundamentals forbidden on our plan). Reopen standard: any short idea pre-registers against the calendar-matched null, not an SPY short alone. Cross-check raised for the long book (untested): random members lagged SPY most in 2019/2023/2024, the long book's lag years. User option (c): the track stays open but idle; short flags stay default-off axes. DEFECTS: 30w-MA float ties (1 event), ticker reuse inside the 120-bar window (ECLP, CCBL, NBIS +7), splices (BELM, CGE), 117 non-common listing events (#3183). Writeup dev/experiments/short-wide-top-2026-10-13/README.md."))
